 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Surjectivity of the multiplication map on points",
 "statement": "Let $A$ be an abelian variety\nover an algebraically closed field $k$ and let $n\\geq1$. Then\n\n$$\n[n]:A(k)\\longrightarrow A(k)\n$$\n\nis surjective.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-abelian-varieties/sk-prop-av-divisible/lem-sc-isogeny-surjective.md",
  "place": "node lem-sc-isogeny-surjective, order 572",
  "external": [
   {
    "document": "Stacks Project",
    "place": "Tag 03RP"
   }
  ]
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sc-abelian-variety",
  "def-sc-mult-n"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [lem-sc-isogeny-facts](a), $[n]$ is a finite flat\nsurjective morphism, so it is surjective on $k$-points by\n[lem-sc-finite-flat-surj-points]\n(*reference: Stacks Project, Groupoid Schemes, Proposition\n39.9.11, parts (3) and (4), [Tag 03RP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03RP): $[n]$ is surjective, and\n$A(k)$ is divisible for $k$ algebraically closed*).",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sc-isogeny-facts",
    "lem-sc-finite-flat-surj-points"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
